      ],
      "content": "TRING                 PARK STREET SP 9211 (South side) 11/103 -                                      Nos. 21, and 22 GV II Block of 2 estate houses.  1880's for Rothschild Estate probably by William Huckvale. Similar to nos. 25, and 26. Plum brick with 1st floor plastered to represent half-timbering,  scalloped red tilehanging to jettied 1st floor to porch, and steep roof of red machine-made tiles. A picturesque 1½ storeys block facing N with central projecting 2-storeys porch open below and second entrance in W end under gabled timber porch. Attic in upper part of roof with gable window. Armorial plaque on porch. 3-light and 2-light casement windows divided. Segmental arches to ground floor, plinth and moulded projecting band below plastered upper part. 2 tall internal chimneys. Listing NGR: SP9253911065"
    }
  ],
